      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The study examines the relative influence of sundry psychological risk factors on the various forms of angina pectoris found in two groups of women with classic angina pains attributable in one group to critical organic lesions of the coronary arteries and in the other to functional spasm. In all 81 women were examined and no significant difference was found between the two groups."},
